          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( \u0915\u0923\u094d\u0921\u0942\u092f\u094d \u0905\u0919\u094d\u0917\u0935\u093f\u0918\u0930\u094d\u0937\u0923\u0947 ). The reading \u0938\u0902\u092a\u0924\u094d\u0938\u094d\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0947 &c. adopted by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"Mr. Telang ( see foot-note ) is more poetical but requires some\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"such expression as \u2018 from me \u2019 to be supplied.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit root and reading are somewhat unclear.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 100. \u092d\u0948\u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u094d\u2014food collected together by begging. \u092d\u0948\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0902\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u092d\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093e\u0915\u0926\u092e\u094d\u092c\u0915\u092e\u094d. Amara. \u0928\u093f\u0903\u0938\u0902\u0917\u0924\u093e &c.\u2014see com.; the develop-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"ment of the mind consisting in renouncing all worldly\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"attachments; or \u0928\u093f\u0938\u094d\u0938\u0902\u0917\u0924\u093e \u0905\u0919\u094d\u0917\u0940\u0915\u0930\u0923\u0938\u094d\u092f \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0923\u0924\u093f\u0903; here \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0923\u0924\u093f means\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"the end, close, or termination; hence the closing act of life.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"When a man has accepted asceticism ( \u0928\u093f\u0903\u0938\u0902\u0917\u0924\u093e ) he has no\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"worldly actions to perform. His accepting asceticism is\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"therefore the last act of his life.\u2014\u0936\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903\u0915\u0930\u0923\u092a\u0930\u093f\u0923\u0924\u093f\u0903 v. l. is to be\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"similarly explained;\u2014\u092a\u0930\u093f\u0923\u0924\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924. is another reading which\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"means\u2014\u0915\u0930\u0923\u0947\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0923\u0924\u0902 \u092f\u0924\u094d\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0902 \u0924\u0947\u0928. \u0938\u0902\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0938\u094d\u0924 &c.\u2014Those who have\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"abandoned ( i. e. got rid of ) the multitudes of contacts ( i. e.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"opportunities ) of self-humiliation ( in supplicating others ).\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"Telang. \u0935\u094d\u092f\u0924\u093f\u0915\u0930 contact, connection; or misfortunes, calamities.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words are indistinct in the scan.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 101. \u092e\u093e\u0924\u0903, \u0924\u093e\u0924 &c.\u2014The Vocatives are significant. See\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"com. The five elements perform the same functions as the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"various relatives mentioned and serve to nourish the body &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0905\u0928\u094d\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0903\u2014last, as I have to take no further birth, ( for he says\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"further on \u2018\u092a\u0930\u0947 \u092c\u094d\u0930\u0939\u094d\u092e\u0923\u093f \u0932\u0940\u092f\u0947\u2019 ) this salutation must be the last from\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"me. \u092f\u0941\u0937\u094d\u092e\u0924\u094d\u0938\u0902\u0917\u0966\u2014for, without the body, formed of the elements,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"he could not have attained the knowledge of Brahma. \u0909\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0947\u0915\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"overflow, abundance \u0932\u0940\u092f\u0947\u2014merge, be absorbed in. This sl.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"forms the fitting conclusion of the S'ataka.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The first Sanskrit term on line 4 is unclear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"heading\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"MISCLLANEOUS.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 1. \u0905\u092e\u094d\u092c\u0930\u0916\u0923\u094d\u0921\u2014(1) a part of the sky; and (2) a strip of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"cloth. \u0938\u0902\u0935\u0940\u0924\u0903\u2014covered, clothed, or surrounded; p. p. of \u0935\u094d\u092f\u0947 with\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0938\u092e\u094d. \u0926\u094c\u0930\u094d\u0917\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0915\u092e\u094d\u2014( \u0926\u0941\u0937\u094d\u091f\u093e \u0917\u0924\u093f\u0903 \u0917\u0924\u0902 \u0935\u093e \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0924\u0938\u094d\u092f \u092d\u093e\u0935\u0903 ) wretchedness. The\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"poet bewails the wretchedness of the sun and the moon who are\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"here described as having but one strip of cloth in common to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"cover themselves with, The fig. here is \u0936\u094d\u0932\u0947\u0937. It is thus defined:-\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0936\u094d\u0932\u0947\u0937\u0903 \u0938 \u0935\u093e\u0915\u094d\u092f \u090f\u0915\u0938\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0924\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0928\u0947\u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0924\u093e \u092d\u0935\u0947\u0924\u094d \u0964 K. P. X. When in the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"same sentence more than one meaning is possible it is \u0936\u094d\u0932\u0947\u0937.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit characters, especially in the definition on line 7, are unclear.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 78 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"100\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"101\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"number\":null,\"label\":\"MISCLLANEOUS.\",\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"1\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]},{\"flow\":\"notes\",\"units\":[]}],\"relations\":[]}"
